# 5. User Management

## Create User

```bash
sudo useradd amit
```

---

## Set Password

```bash
sudo passwd amit
```

---

## User Information

```bash
id amit
```

---

## Current Logged-in Users

```bash
who
```

---

## User Details

```bash
cat /etc/passwd
```

---

# 6. Sudo Privileges

Grant sudo access:

Ubuntu

```bash
sudo usermod -aG sudo amit
```

RHEL / Amazon Linux

```bash
sudo usermod -aG wheel amit
```

---

# 7. SSH Authentication

## Generate SSH Key Pair

```bash
ssh-keygen
```

Generates:

```
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
```

---

## Public Key

Stored on the server:

```
~/.ssh/authorized_keys
```

---

## Private Key

Stored securely on your local machine.

Never share it.

---

## Connect via SSH

```bash
ssh -i key.pem ec2-user@<public-ip>
```

---

# 8. Bastion Host

A Bastion Host (Jump Server) is used to securely access private servers.

```
Laptop
      │
      ▼
 Bastion Host
      │
      ▼
 Private Server
```

### Benefits

- No direct SSH access to private servers
- Centralized access management
- Improved security
- Audit logging

